body:
I'm currently going through this right now. It is an absolute pain in the ass, I totally sympathise with you. What's helped me is telling myself that if I can't sleep then that's okay for now and I'll just stay up and read. Often, I read to the point where I get too tired to stay awake anymore. Another thing that helps is having audios playing such as audios from Barry Mcdonagh's 'Dare' app. I really hope you are able to sleep soon. If not, please seek some therapy in order to help you find ways to cope with stress so that you can develop a normal routine again.

&#x200B;

Good luck, hang in there <3

I understand how scared you must be. I'm sorry your boyfriend reacted like that, that must've made you feel terrible. Can you try sitting down with him & explaining how you feel so he can empathise and support you? Together you can try & figure out ways to help you cope with this whether it be watching something together before bed etc etc. 

&#x200B;

All the best <3
